<DemoExample Title="Basic" RazorCode="@example1RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example1CsharpCode" Id="example1">
    <div>
        Any class feeds the breadcrumb: <b>NameSelectors</b> maps its properties by selector or by name. A mapped
        <b>Href</b> makes a link; the <b>IsSelected</b> mapping marks the current page (<code>aria-current="page"</code>)
        and <b>SelectedItemAsText</b> renders it as plain text. <b>IsEnabled</b> disables the whole trail or a single item,
        and a <b>Target</b> mapping opens a link elsewhere (with <code>rel="noopener noreferrer"</code>).
    </div>
    <br />
    <div class="example-box">
        <div>
            <div>Basic</div>
            <BitBreadcrumb Items="CustomBreadcrumbItems" NameSelectors="nameSelectors" />
        </div>
        <div>
            <div>Selected item as text</div>
            <BitBreadcrumb Items="CustomBreadcrumbItems" NameSelectors="nameSelectors" SelectedItemAsText />
        </div>
        <div>
            <div>Disabled</div>
            <BitBreadcrumb Items="CustomBreadcrumbItems" NameSelectors="nameSelectors" IsEnabled="false" />
        </div>
        <div>
            <div>Item disabled</div>
            <BitBreadcrumb Items="CustomBreadcrumbItemsDisabled" NameSelectors="nameSelectors" />
        </div>
        <div>
            <div>Item target (opens in a new tab)</div>
            <BitBreadcrumb Items="CustomBreadcrumbItemsWithTarget" NameSelectors="nameSelectors" />
        </div>
    </div>
</DemoExample>

<DemoExample Title="MaxDisplayedItems & OverflowIndex" RazorCode="@example2RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example2CsharpCode" Id="example2">
    <div>
        <b>MaxDisplayedItems</b> caps the visible items and collapses the rest into an overflow menu; <b>OverflowIndex</b>
        places its button. Keyboard: Enter, Space or the arrows open the menu, arrows and Home/End move, a letter jumps to
        the matching item, Escape or Tab closes it.
    </div>
    <br />
    <div class="example-box">
        <div>
            <div>Max displayed items (2)</div>
            <BitBreadcrumb Items="CustomBreadcrumbItems" NameSelectors="nameSelectors" MaxDisplayedItems="2" />
        </div>
        <div>
            <div>Max displayed items (3), Overflow index (1)</div>
            <BitBreadcrumb Items="CustomBreadcrumbItems" NameSelectors="nameSelectors" MaxDisplayedItems="3" OverflowIndex="1" />
        </div>
        <div>
            <div>Max displayed items (3), Overflow index (2)</div>
            <BitBreadcrumb Items="CustomBreadcrumbItems" NameSelectors="nameSelectors" MaxDisplayedItems="3" OverflowIndex="2" />
        </div>
    </div>
</DemoExample>

<DemoExample Title="Truncation, Wrapping & Scrolling" RazorCode="@example3RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example3CsharpCode" Id="example3">
    <div>
        A long trail stays on one line by default. <b>MaxItemWidth</b> truncates each item (its text becomes the tooltip
        when it has no mapped <b>Title</b>), <b>Wrap</b> flows it onto more lines and <b>Scrollable</b> scrolls it sideways.
    </div>
    <br />
    <div class="example-box">
        <div>
            <div>Default (single line)</div>
            <div class="narrow-box">
                <BitBreadcrumb Items="CustomBreadcrumbItemsWithLongText" NameSelectors="nameSelectors" />
            </div>
        </div>
        <div>
            <div>MaxItemWidth</div>
            <div class="narrow-box">
                <BitBreadcrumb Items="CustomBreadcrumbItemsWithLongText" NameSelectors="nameSelectors" MaxItemWidth="5rem" />
            </div>
        </div>
        <div>
            <div>Wrap</div>
            <div class="narrow-box">
                <BitBreadcrumb Items="CustomBreadcrumbItemsWithLongText" NameSelectors="nameSelectors" Wrap />
            </div>
        </div>
        <div>
            <div>Scrollable</div>
            <div class="narrow-box">
                <BitBreadcrumb Items="CustomBreadcrumbItemsWithLongText" NameSelectors="nameSelectors" Scrollable />
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</DemoExample>

<DemoExample Title="Auto Collapse" RazorCode="@example4RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example4CsharpCode" Id="example4">
    <div>
        <b>AutoCollapse</b> moves what does not fit into the overflow menu and brings it back as room returns.
        MaxDisplayedItems and OverflowIndex still apply; Wrap turns it off.
    </div>
    <br />
    <div class="example-box">
        <div>
            <div>Drag the bottom-right corner of the box to resize it</div>
            <div class="resizable-box">
                <BitBreadcrumb Items="CustomBreadcrumbItemsWithLongText" NameSelectors="nameSelectors" AutoCollapse />
            </div>
        </div>
        <div>
            <div>Overflow index (1): the root stays, the middle collapses</div>
            <div class="resizable-box">
                <BitBreadcrumb Items="CustomBreadcrumbItemsWithLongText" NameSelectors="nameSelectors" AutoCollapse OverflowIndex="1" />
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</DemoExample>

<DemoExample Title="Expand Overflow" RazorCode="@example5RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example5CsharpCode" Id="example5">
    <div>
        <b>ExpandOverflow</b> makes the overflow button reveal the collapsed items in place instead of opening a menu, and
        moves the focus to the first revealed item. Pair it with Wrap or Scrollable when room is tight.
    </div>
    <br />
    <div class="example-box">
        <div>
            <div>Expand in place</div>
            <BitBreadcrumb Items="CustomBreadcrumbItemsWithControlled" NameSelectors="nameSelectors" ExpandOverflow MaxDisplayedItems="3" OverflowIndex="1" />
        </div>
        <div>
            <div>Expand and wrap in a narrow container</div>
            <div class="narrow-box">
                <BitBreadcrumb Items="CustomBreadcrumbItemsWithLongText" NameSelectors="nameSelectors" ExpandOverflow Wrap MaxDisplayedItems="2" OverflowIndex="1" />
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</DemoExample>

<DemoExample Title="Icons & Divider" RazorCode="@example6RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example6CsharpCode" Id="example6">
    <div>
        The <b>IconName</b> mapping adds an icon to an item and <b>ReversedIcon</b> puts it after the text. An icon-only
        item needs an <b>AriaLabel</b> mapping. <b>DividerIconName</b>, <b>DividerText</b> and <b>OverflowIconName</b>
        replace the default glyphs; dividers are always hidden from screen readers.
    </div>
    <br />
    <div class="example-box">
        <div>
            <div>Item icons, DividerIconName & OverflowIconName</div>
            <BitBreadcrumb Items="CustomBreadcrumbItemsWithIcon"
                           NameSelectors="nameSelectors"
                           DividerIconName="@BitIconName.CaretRightSolid8"
                           OverflowIconName="@BitIconName.ChevronDown"
                           MaxDisplayedItems="3"
                           OverflowIndex="2" />
        </div>
        <div>
            <div>ReversedIcon</div>
            <BitBreadcrumb Items="CustomBreadcrumbItemsWithIcon" NameSelectors="nameSelectors" ReversedIcon />
        </div>
        <div>
            <div>Icon-only root with an AriaLabel & DividerText</div>
            <BitBreadcrumb Items="CustomBreadcrumbItemsWithHomeIcon" NameSelectors="nameSelectors" DividerText="/" />
        </div>
    </div>
</DemoExample>

<DemoExample Title="Templates" RazorCode="@example7RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example7CsharpCode" Id="example7">
    <div>
        <b>DividerIconTemplate</b>, <b>ItemTemplate</b> and <b>OverflowTemplate</b> customize every item; the
        <b>Template</b> and <b>OverflowTemplate</b> mapped on an item win over them.
    </div>
    <br />
    <div class="example-box">
        <div>
            <div>DividerIconTemplate</div>
            <BitBreadcrumb Items="CustomBreadcrumbItems" NameSelectors="nameSelectors">
                <DividerIconTemplate>
                    <BitIcon IconName="@BitIconName.CaretRightSolid8" Color="BitColor.Warning" />
                </DividerIconTemplate>
            </BitBreadcrumb>
        </div>
        <div>
            <div>ItemTemplate & OverflowTemplate</div>
            <BitBreadcrumb Items="CustomBreadcrumbItems" NameSelectors="nameSelectors" MaxDisplayedItems="3" OverflowIndex="2">
                <ItemTemplate Context="item">
                    <div style="font-weight: bold; color: #d13438; font-style: italic;">
                        @item.Name
                    </div>
                </ItemTemplate>
                <OverflowTemplate Context="item">
                    <div style="font-weight: bold; color: blueviolet; font-style: italic;">
                        @item.Name
                    </div>
                </OverflowTemplate>
            </BitBreadcrumb>
        </div>
        <div>
            <div>Item's Template & OverflowTemplate</div>
            <BitBreadcrumb Items="CustomBreadcrumbItemTemplateItems" NameSelectors="nameSelectors" MaxDisplayedItems="3" OverflowIndex="2" />
        </div>
    </div>
</DemoExample>

<DemoExample Title="Events & Dynamic Items" RazorCode="@example8RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example8CsharpCode" Id="example8">
    <div>
        <b>OnItemClick</b> reports every activated item, link or button (the NameSelectors' <b>OnClick</b> adds a per-item
        handler). Here it moves the selection, while the items and the collapsing settings change at runtime.
    </div>
    <br />
    <div class="example-box">
        <BitBreadcrumb Items="CustomBreadcrumbItemsWithCustomized"
                       NameSelectors="nameSelectors"
                       MaxDisplayedItems="@MaxDisplayedItems"
                       OverflowIndex="@OverflowIndex"
                       OnItemClick="(PageInfo model) => HandleOnCustomizedCustomClick(model)"
                       Styles="@(new() { SelectedItem = "color: dodgerblue;", OverflowSelectedItem = "color: red;" })" />
        <div class="operators">
            <div>
                <BitButton OnClick="AddCustomItem">Add item</BitButton>
                <BitButton OnClick="RemoveCustomItem">Remove item</BitButton>
            </div>
            <BitNumberField @bind-Value="MaxDisplayedItems" Label="Max displayed items" ShowButtons />
            <BitNumberField @bind-Value="OverflowIndex" Label="Overflow index" ShowButtons />
        </div>
    </div>
</DemoExample>

<DemoExample Title="Structured Data" RazorCode="@example9RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example9CsharpCode" Id="example9">
    <div>
        <b>StructuredData</b> renders the whole trail, collapsed items included, as a schema.org <code>BreadcrumbList</code>
        JSON-LD script with absolute URLs for search engines. Inspect the page to see it.
    </div>
    <br />
    <div class="example-box">
        <BitBreadcrumb Items="CustomBreadcrumbItems" NameSelectors="nameSelectors" StructuredData MaxDisplayedItems="3" OverflowIndex="2" />
    </div>
</DemoExample>

<DemoExample Title="Cascading parameters" RazorCode="@example10RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example10CsharpCode" Id="example10">
    <div>
        <b>BitParams</b> hands a <b>BitBreadcrumbParams</b> to every breadcrumb under it, whatever its item type. The values
        are defaults, not overrides: a parameter a breadcrumb sets itself wins.
    </div>
    <br />
    <div class="example-box">
        <BitParams Parameters="@breadcrumbParams">
            <div>
                <div>Takes the divider, the collapsing and the plain text current page from the cascade</div>
                <BitBreadcrumb Items="CustomBreadcrumbItems" NameSelectors="nameSelectors" />
            </div>
            <div>
                <div>Its own divider, the cascaded rest</div>
                <BitBreadcrumb Items="CustomBreadcrumbItems" NameSelectors="nameSelectors" DividerText="›" />
            </div>
        </BitParams>
        <div>
            <div>Outside the cascade, back to the defaults</div>
            <BitBreadcrumb Items="CustomBreadcrumbItems" NameSelectors="nameSelectors" />
        </div>
    </div>
</DemoExample>

